#!  conjecture_proved(?Point, ?Template, ?Argument)
#
#   The conjectures proved on 2026-09-28, each by at least one proof
#   reviewed step by step, a paper proof not in this repository; they are
#   proved claims. The
#   proofs are of consistency with lambda beta eta, which
#   implies consistency with lambda beta (every equation lambda beta proves,
#   lambda beta eta proves), so they stand under a judgment over lambda
#   beta and under a judgment over lambda beta eta.
#   Reviewed class by class for lambda beta eta, 2026-09-29; each class has at least one accepted proof
#   whose collapsing rule is shown to commute with eta:
#   - fixpoint_collapse: eta in the decreasing diagram, by Hindley-Rosen,
#     or commuting with the collapse;
#   - safety_collapse and comparison_collapse: a theorem whose set is
#     closed under eta, and a collapse lemma with eta by Hindley's lemma;
#     safety_escape_behind_traps also by two proofs over lambda beta eta;
#   - subtype_collapse: the same theorem, whose set is closed under eta;
#   - certificate_collapse, the cycles of any Count included: the
#     certificate proofs state lambda beta eta plus the collapse;
#   - respelled_collapse: two of its proofs are over lambda beta eta (a
#     third is over lambda beta alone and is not needed).
#   The class easy (`contest_easy_terms.pl`) rests on
#   `doc/proofs/omega_easy_beta_eta.md`. Every proof
#   adds, to beta and eta, a rule collapsing a set of
#   closed terms that contains the point's term (or a reduct of it) onto the
#   value, and shows the extended reduction confluent with true and false
#   distinct normal forms:
#
#   - fixpoint_collapse: M = Y G with G = \x. x B1 ... Bk, and false
#     B1[false] ... Bk[false] reduces to false (H29, H30);
#   - comparison_collapse: the left-first comparison of two left spines
#     (H15), false carried by the conjunction with the right subtrees'
#     comparison;
#   - safety_collapse: safe on an infinite good path, either boolean
#     carried by the or over the successors (H4, H5, H14), the traps of
#     safety_escape_behind_traps refuted by beta;
#   - subtype_collapse: the recursive subtype check, either boolean carried
#     by the conjunction over the supertype's fields (H2, H19).
#
#   The certificate points H22 and H24 are proved by
#   certificate_collapse, at the class (`cycle_claim/4`); the twin's traps
#   stay conjectures.
#
#   Proved later, and proved claims:
#
#   - respelled_collapse: boolean(false) of the three respelled cycles
#     (`contest_respelled_cycles.pl`; `doc/proofs/kestrel_respelled_cycles_family.md`,
#     `heron_respelled_family.md`, `individual_respelled_cycles_consistency.md`);
#   - certificate_collapse extended to a cycle of any Count >= 1 members, at
#     the class certificate_cycle (`contest_certificate_cycles.pl`;
#     `doc/proofs/certificate_cycles.md`, `osprey_certificate_cycle_collapse.md`,
#     `individual_certificate_cycles_consistency.md`).
#
#   Proved later still, and proved claims:
#
#   - arithmetic_search: both booleans of the three arithmetic theorems
#     (`contest_arithmetic_theorems.pl`;
#     `doc/proofs/arithmetic_search_consistency.md`, for the linear
#     fragment the three theorems belong to);
#   - continuation_eta_omega: both booleans of continuation_true_eta
#     (`contest_continuation_cycles.pl`;
#     `doc/proofs/continuation_true_eta_is_omega.md`);
#   - continuation_projection_collapse: the scored claims of the other five
#     continuation points (`doc/proofs/continuation_projection_collapse.md`).
#
# The template is a constructor of schema/template, a Boolean a Church
# Boolean of corpora/library/prelude/boolean. Each other text is from_cbor
# of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes, imported from
# corpora/library/text/cbor. FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
